# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/
# mypy is configured in pyproject.toml ([tool.mypy]), so this directory was
# always going to appear -- it was simply missing here until it did. Stage 3
# had to untrack committed __pycache__ bytecode; catching this one before
# anything was tracked is the cheaper version of the same fix.
.mypy_cache/

# Local backup / scratch files
*.bak
*.orig
*.Rhistory
terrium_data_flow.html

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Env / secrets
.env
*.env.local

# Word temp/lock files
~$*.docx

.gstack/

# Installed dependencies, anywhere in the tree.
#
# The root package.json ("terrium-scientific-backend", which drives src/
# and examples/) needs its own node_modules, and until 2026-08-10 nothing
# ignored it: `git status` listed it as untracked, so a `git add -A` would
# have committed tens of thousands of vendored files. The rule below is
# unanchored deliberately -- it matches node_modules at any depth, so a new
# workspace is covered the moment it exists rather than when someone
# remembers to add a line here.
node_modules/

# Coverage output from `npm run test:coverage`.
coverage/

# Compiled TypeScript output. `tsconfig.json` gained an `outDir` so that
# `npm run build` emits somewhere, and 41 compiled .js files were committed
# on 2026-08-11 -- a duplicate of every source file in the tree, which goes
# stale the moment anyone edits the TypeScript and gives a reader a second,
# wrong answer to "what does this module do". Build output is derived, not
# source.
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Science-Agent-Pipeline is folded into this repo as regular files (it used
# to be tracked as a gitlink to its own separate repo, which broke CI --
# GitHub Actions checkout tried to resolve the gitlink and there was no
# .gitmodules pointing anywhere real). Its own node_modules/build output are
# covered by Science-Agent-Pipeline/.gitignore; this repo's pnpm store cache
# (created while verifying the merge) should never be committed either.
.pnpm-store/

# Marketing site — lives in its own repo (see site/README.md)
site/

# Local coding-agent tool state -- not source, and not small (FreeBuff's
# own working directory has been observed at tens of MB locally). Never
# belongs in the repo regardless of which tool produced it.
.freebuff/
.aider.chat.history.md
.aider*.json

# Coverage artifacts (binary sqlite, regenerated by `coverage run`)
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.mutate-journal/

# Confidential internal documents. Every file in Docw/ is marked
# "Confidential" on its own pages and one is also "Internal Use Only";
# they were published in a public repository until 2026-08-16. Kept on
# disk, out of the repository. See the commit that removed them.
Docw/
Science-Agent-Pipeline/attached_assets/*.docx
